# MAYOTIX OS Phase 3 Week 2: Bubblewrap Profile for Network-Isolated CLI Tools
# This profile is for offline tools that do not require network access.
# It sets up a sandbox with no network namespace (unshare-net) and no network access.

# We source this file in mayotix-bwrap.sh, so we set variables that will be used.

# Override the network option to 'none' (which is the default, but we make it explicit)
NETWORK="none"

# Optionally, we can also drop more capabilities or adjust mounts.
# For network-isolated, we might want to drop even more, but the default in mayotix-bwrap.sh is to drop all capabilities.
# We can leave it as is, or explicitly set to drop all (already done by --cap-all if CAPABILITIES is not set).

# If we want to allow only specific capabilities, we can set CAPABILITIES here.
# For a completely isolated offline tool, we might not need any capabilities.
# So we leave CAPABILITIES unset to drop all.

# Note: The script already sets up a minimal read-only root, private /tmp, and isolated /home.
# This profile just ensures network is isolated.